{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","id":"pg_0bd31303bb0559f1ac62e28279496479","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gsa-tts-agentic-coding-quickstart-support-md-e0b9a3b60d87-e28279496479.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a6700e2bb5ed5889911838a390b707ca"],"title":"GSA-TTS/agentic-coding-quickstart/SUPPORT.md @ e0b9a3b60d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_21bcf4ec6d99827d6cc427fcbe821fefc06ff85f931d7ca018065f7ca40a9173"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"msb cannot mount symlinked host paths (failing with 'Not a directory'), so acq canonicalizes workspaces; macOS $TMPDIR paths under /var fail unless resolved to /private/var."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3cced06c7f668f2b0f0390a590ce4801bd68a187f4ad2e5dc57de66f03774dc1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Backend selection is exposed via `acq backend set <name>`, a per-invocation `--backend` flag, and the `ACQ_BACKEND` environment variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_632bea2423d1c83f8de31755260d4da72e9db51225a57dec581c0e1e7ac23330"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A backend-neutral custom base image can be set with `--image` or `ACQ_IMAGE`; precedence is flag > env > backend-specific variable, and an explicitly set `ACQ_MSB_IMAGE` wins over the neutral knob with a notice."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6722ca9a4503e8da86de84d6c4fb2cb0f3f50c9690a92fca3f352b422c374fdc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Although microsandbox has a snapshot CLI, acq does not surface it, so `ACQ_BACKEND_SUPPORTS_SNAPSHOTS=0` reflects what acq exposes rather than msb's capability."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6a20a6de2f79815591eb74c0197bc0ed37078855cf33ec492ab6fa37bcd9382e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sbx backend requires the sbx CLI >= 0.38.0 (for the v2 kit grammar) plus a Docker account, while the msb backend requires msb >= 0.6.8 and host virtualization (KVM, Apple Silicon HVF, or Windows WHP)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_716833d4b1537dab00f86cfb1764f13d54581aed86f384bc781595fc1b9a8727"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"acq supports two shipped isolation backends: msb (microsandbox, a lightweight open-source microVM runtime, the default) and sbx (Docker Sandboxes), with a Podman-based 'ppp' backend listed as in development."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e0680100f3993f23071f16f3890eab718e31ca70b9dc01015d27ff26813b1b0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On sbx 0.38, `sbx kit add` cannot apply startup-bearing kits to a live sandbox, so the built-in kit bundle can only be extended by recreating the sandbox; msb is unaffected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0ba634522f37ab024d8e9e5d7d8dc6b73299a4817392db6862c88ffdc5bf36c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Secrets are injected at runtime via a proxy/host-env binding (e.g. `--secret USAI_API_KEY@api.gsa.usai.gov`), so real secret values never enter the guest VM or container."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d58b51a625f9387cadaee2583fe719821051e98f6e17166bf76b499279253cf7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Network egress is selected by a backend-neutral tier variable `ACQ_NETWORK_TIER` (strict, balanced, open; default balanced); strict and balanced are deny-by-default with allowlists, and `open` requires an explicit confirmation variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ec67fd4b090e8fa5fbcf3e8e84a541fd305328395e2b4e7bc51572c2050a0fad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The msb backend defaults sandboxes to 4 GiB RAM and 2 vCPUs (overriding msb's 512 MiB/1 vCPU, which OOM-kills Node TUI agents), tunable via ACQ_MSB_MEMORY/ACQ_MSB_CPUS."}],"claim_ids":["clm_21bcf4ec6d99827d6cc427fcbe821fefc06ff85f931d7ca018065f7ca40a9173","clm_3cced06c7f668f2b0f0390a590ce4801bd68a187f4ad2e5dc57de66f03774dc1","clm_632bea2423d1c83f8de31755260d4da72e9db51225a57dec581c0e1e7ac23330","clm_6722ca9a4503e8da86de84d6c4fb2cb0f3f50c9690a92fca3f352b422c374fdc","clm_6a20a6de2f79815591eb74c0197bc0ed37078855cf33ec492ab6fa37bcd9382e","clm_716833d4b1537dab00f86cfb1764f13d54581aed86f384bc781595fc1b9a8727","clm_7e0680100f3993f23071f16f3890eab718e31ca70b9dc01015d27ff26813b1b0","clm_d0ba634522f37ab024d8e9e5d7d8dc6b73299a4817392db6862c88ffdc5bf36c","clm_d58b51a625f9387cadaee2583fe719821051e98f6e17166bf76b499279253cf7","clm_ec67fd4b090e8fa5fbcf3e8e84a541fd305328395e2b4e7bc51572c2050a0fad"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","id":"pg_1dcf8733542c58459c2e28c997a00f03","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gsa-tts-agentic-coding-quickstart-docs-backend-guide-md-e0b9a3b60d87-28c997a00f03.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"title":"GSA-TTS/agentic-coding-quickstart/docs/BACKEND_GUIDE.md @ e0b9a3b60d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_48943dbfaf9facae9d6e09e77b8c14547c34dddc49d9c1ff44dad1ca2ba20608"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product's entry point is the `acq` CLI, invoked e.g. as `acq run opencode ~/my-project`, which runs the agent in a sandbox configured for federal usage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_716833d4b1537dab00f86cfb1764f13d54581aed86f384bc781595fc1b9a8727"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"acq supports two shipped isolation backends: msb (microsandbox, a lightweight open-source microVM runtime, the default) and sbx (Docker Sandboxes), with a Podman-based 'ppp' backend listed as in development."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4600bd06623848c727681178028fff7c21b85aef18643951c0cd1620d0e77eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The quickstart targets federal teams using AI coding agents, connecting them to USAi (GSA's LLM gateway at api.gsa.usai.gov), and is classified as a local development environment for Low/Moderate-impact work, not a production/hosted environment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0ba634522f37ab024d8e9e5d7d8dc6b73299a4817392db6862c88ffdc5bf36c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Secrets are injected at runtime via a proxy/host-env binding (e.g. `--secret USAI_API_KEY@api.gsa.usai.gov`), so real secret values never enter the guest VM or container."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eaefae11f3ee353787874776163f43a32a7ef20b75c67b93c73163277bb12d99"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The companion playbook provides agent skills following the agentskills.io standard (e.g. federal-security-controls-lookup, ato-package, code-review), symlinked into ~/.agents/skills when a sandbox launches so agents discover them automatically."}],"claim_ids":["clm_48943dbfaf9facae9d6e09e77b8c14547c34dddc49d9c1ff44dad1ca2ba20608","clm_716833d4b1537dab00f86cfb1764f13d54581aed86f384bc781595fc1b9a8727","clm_a4600bd06623848c727681178028fff7c21b85aef18643951c0cd1620d0e77eb","clm_d0ba634522f37ab024d8e9e5d7d8dc6b73299a4817392db6862c88ffdc5bf36c","clm_eaefae11f3ee353787874776163f43a32a7ef20b75c67b93c73163277bb12d99"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","id":"pg_277204203f9c5027a6d2b8e5165758c3","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gsa-tts-agentic-coding-quickstart-readme-md-e0b9a3b60d87-b8e5165758c3.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d"],"title":"GSA-TTS/agentic-coding-quickstart/README.md @ e0b9a3b60d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
